+"""W6C-B13: a book we could not look at must not print as a book we looked at — POSITION READBACK
+OBSERVABILITY, and the non-flattening response to it.
+
+*** MOCK ONLY: MockBroker, temp state dirs, pilot_log trees copied from the REAL committed day
+    state/live/pilot_log/20260801 into tmp. No venue, no credentials, no network, nothing written
+    under state/. ***
+
+THE DEFECT (quant_research docs/fixprogram_2026-09-13/FX_W6C/FACT_TABLE_B13.md): all three position
+guards answer "is the book where we think it is" from whichever anchor last carried a readback, and
+none of them compares that against the newest anchor that actually happened.
+  · §4-5b  watchdog.py:1907 `last_reconciled_ats = _rec["last_reconciled_ats"]`, and reconcile()
+           iterates ONLY anchors that appear in position_readback rows (reconcile.py:701-708), so an
+           anchor without one is not in its domain. `blind` (:1996) is True only when there is no
+           reconciliation in the WHOLE window.
+  · §4-5e  position_break.py:890 `latest = judged[-1]`; a readback-less anchor is `NO_READBACK`,
+           `judged=False` (:702) and is skipped. `blind` (:911) cannot be True while any older
+           anchor was judged.
+  · §4-7   watchdog_inputs.py:114-116 reads the same reconciliation.
+Measured on ef60f85 by devices/probe_unreadable_book.py cell U1: the newest anchor wrote no readback
+⇒ not tripped, `conditions_blind []`, 5b CLEAN on the PREVIOUS anchor, 5e CLEAN, cond7 drift CLEAN.
+Judged on stale state, reported as checked-and-clean.
+
+THE RESPONSE, and the rule it obeys (user 2026-09-12, memory feedback_no_book_level_response_to_
+instrument_doubt): an instrument's own doubt must never trigger a book-level response. So the answer
+to "we cannot see the book" is: name the blind state, HALT OPENING, page — and flatten NOTHING. Cost
+of a false positive: one anchor of skipped opening trades, book held, reduce-only paths still run.
+
+WHAT THIS SUITE PROVES, on this tree:
+  [A] the headline and its neighbours, on the REAL 20260801 rows re-shaped: the newest scheduled
+      anchor's readback removed ⇒ every guard names it and goes blind, and NOTHING is flattened
+      (base ef60f85 prints CLEAN and not blind — red for the right reason).
+  [N] negative controls, green on BOTH trees: the untouched real day; the day including its real
+      20:19Z FLATTEN pair (whose readback lands 0.131 s later under its own key — 10/10 batches in
+      the live record have this shape, so a naive `max(anchor_ts)` reference would halt after every
+      trip); the real HOLD-anchor shape (2026-08-29 20Z: readback, no `anchors` row); a tree with no
+      readback at all (the DRY_RUN shape) which must stay exactly as blind as it is today and must
+      NOT halt; and four book-level triggers that must still flatten everything.
+  [P] the producer's own verdict — finalize_anchor is the only code that knows WHY there are no
+      rows, and today read-failure / no-account / empty-universe / truncated-write all print as
+      "no rows".
+  [G] the gate: anchor_loop.book_unobserved_halt — halts opening, never flattens, never sets
+      reduce-only, fail-closed on an unreadable file, silent on an absent one.
+  [W] the wiring, statically: run_anchor passes the producer's verdict; the anchors row carries the
+      held-book halt kind so §4-5e does not judge the halted anchor against intent ZERO and trip the
+      ladder one anchor later (the B14 lesson from EXE-01).
+WHAT IT DOES NOT PROVE: that an anchor which dies before phase C is detectable (it leaves no row of
+any kind — the 2026-09-09 12Z anchor is absent from the record entirely; that is the off-box
+deadman's question, FACT_TABLE_B13 §7); the venue's behaviour under any of this; off-box delivery.
+
+Old-code proof: this file on ef60f85 must REACH its summary line — every new name is looked up with
+getattr/.get — and fail the [A]/[P]/[G]/[W] cells for the right reason.
